course: dictionary
lesson: 12430
title: Deceit and tricks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deceit means making someone believe something that is not true, to trick them. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The fox used deceit to get into the hen house.» The clue is the trick: the fox made the hens believe it was safe, so deceit must mean tricking someone.
explain: Deceit is a noun you cannot count, so you say «some deceit», not «two deceits». But a deceit is one trick or lie, so you can say «a deceit». To check your meaning, swap in trick or lie: if the sentence still makes sense, you have got it.
explain: Deceit shows up in stories and in friendship. The wolf's deceit in fairy tales and Jacob's deceit in a Bible story are both about tricking someone. Friends value honesty because deceit breaks trust.
fact: Deceit means making someone believe something that is not true, to trick them.
fact: A deceit is a trick or lie, so you can say «a deceit» for one trick.
fact: Deceit is uncountable as a noun: say «some deceit», not «two deceits».
fact: In fairy tales, the wolf uses deceit to trick Red Riding Hood.
fact: Honesty is the opposite of deceit.
exercise: «The fox used deceit to get into the hen house.» What does deceit mean here? | Being open and honest about a plan | Running very fast to escape | *Making someone believe something that is not true, to trick them
exercise: «Her smile was a deceit; she had hidden the broken vase.» In this sentence, what is a deceit? | A broken vase | *A trick or lie | A kind of smile | A sunny day
exercise: «Honesty is the opposite of deceit.» Which word is the opposite of deceit? | Disguise | Trick | Lie | *Honesty
test: «Jacob used deceit to trick his blind father.» What did Jacob do? | He sang his father a song | *He tricked his father into believing something untrue | He ran away from home | He helped his father to see
test: «The wolf put on Grandma's nightcap and used deceit to fool Red Riding Hood.» Which word means the same as deceit here? | Music | Sleep | Kindness | *Trick
exam: Why is deceit a problem in friendship? | Because friends must always be quiet | Because it is a kind of weather | Because it makes friends taller | *Because it breaks trust
